A||||28||DreXteR||Bore 0.060 + turbo = overkill?||||4||
Z||000000||DreXteR||01-09-2001||08:28 AM||||I found a 3.2 flat pistons with 8.3 compression, but 4 use it the block will need to be bored 0.060 over.  In the future willbe a turbo upgrade, I dont know if this combination is an overkill!!  Maybe the block can crack by the presure that will recive.  Im planinig to to 15 psi of boost and maybe something else. Need advise!!   <P><BR>Thanx.||||reg||4
Z||000001||1FST2M6||01-09-2001||09:09 AM||||you should be ok.. running 1bar really isn't all that much boost espescially with that low of a C/R. just make sure it's intercooled.. if not you'll just be wasting your time and loosing all the HP to heat. stay away from Total seal rings a decent cro-moly is just fine.. and if you plan on only..  racing cast rings are killer and will GLADLY except the boost. but won't handle nitrous they like hypereutectic pistons will shatter with any sudden intake difference.. in temp. What kinda pistons are you running? Hypereutectic are great for turbo cars but stay away from nitrous and turbo with them.. a good forged slug would be able to handle the nos and turbo with less problems. <A HREF="http://www.nitrous.org" TARGET=_blank>www.nitrous.org</A>  water injection is another way to lower your intake charge temps. with that much boost heat from the turbo discharge is gunna be your only real concern. Copper head gaskets from Paeco in birmingham, Al. for $60 ea are bullet proof and available in different thicknesse to drop the C/R even more. an MSD 6BTM and vortech SFMU for ign and fuel. or a LINK or Haltech E6GM. but they aren't a must.<P>(oops wrong link)<p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 01-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||1FST2M6||01-09-2001||09:16 AM||||from <A HREF="http://www.nitrous.org" TARGET=_blank>www.nitrous.org</A>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><BR>You Know You Have Too Much Horsepower When.. 1. The emissions test guy starts laughing as soon as you pull onto the rollers.<BR>2. You can't drive your car in the rain.<BR>3. Your 'significant other' is afraid to drive your car.<BR>4. You are afraid to drive your car.<BR>5. You spend more on tires than on food.<BR>6. You spend more on car insurance than on house payments.<BR>7. You look in a state police car and see a picture of your car taped to the dash.<BR>8. You throw your underwear in the garbage rather than the hamper.<BR>9. You have to go to the track to buy gas.<BR>10. Your mechanic names the new wing of his shop after you.<BR>11. Jacques Villeneuve and Michael Schumacher wave you by.<BR>12. You can make the Kessel Run in less than 12 parsecs.<BR>13. You're tempted to wear your fire suit just to drive to the office.<BR>14. Red signal lights shift to green as you're approaching then shift back to red as you're receding.<BR>15. You arrive somewhere before you left.<BR>16. You get pulled over for doing 155 in a 35 but the cops will let you go if "they can look under the hood."<BR>17. You remove the $2000 stereo system to save 6 lb. of weight.<BR>18. You are not allowed to run in the Silver State Challenge.<BR>19. You get an anonymous phone call asking if you are interested in being in the Cannonball Run.<BR>20. Your face looks like you are riding a NASA centrifuge when you drive the car.<BR>22. You need parachute braking.<BR>23. 'significant other' won't even ride in the car.<BR>24 There is no possible way to "sneak out" of your neighborhood at 6 am.<BR>25. Your pets scramble for their hiding spots as soon as the garage door is opened. (Pets, and all the neighbors...)<BR>26. Family photos throughout the house are replaced with ife-sized posters of your car.<BR>27. Fuel is delivered to your home: in 55 gallon drums!<BR>28. You carry earplugs in your car.(doesn't everybody???)<BR>29. The only spot on the car which receives any regular cleaning is the windshield. (what else is there to clean???)<BR>30. You find out that side mirrors don't hold up at speeds exceeding 145 mph.<BR>31. Young children cling to their mommies in fear when you round the corner.<BR>32. Birds fall out of their nests from the rumble of your 5" dual exhaust.<BR>33. All the major Tire makers are sending you free slicks in hopes of endorsment deal.<BR>34. The UPS guy took to taking Steroids so he could keep up with your shipments.<BR>35. The Fed Ex guy had a nervous breakdown.<BR>36. All the wildlife within a 800ft radius around your house got the HELLOUT.<BR>37. The nearest Geological Seismic Surveying Station Operator knows your address by heart.<BR>38. A booming voice greets potential passengers with, "That's right....you paid for the whole seat but you'll only need the EDGE.<BR>39. The earth slows in rotation when you hook up on your new slicks and head east now thats.<BR>40. You have to screw your slicks to the wheels.<BR>41. Your exhaust pipes are larger in diameter than your driveline.<BR>42. Your fuel pump flows enough to water a golf course.<BR>43. Your compression's high enough you could run diesel fuel.<BR>44. The sparks from your wheelie bars start grass fires on the side of the road.<BR>45. Your engine idles at 2800 rpm.<BR>46. You measure the fuel you use in "gallons per mile.<BR> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Will||01-09-2001||09:37 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 1FST2M6:<BR><B><BR>You Know You Have Too Much Horsepower When.. <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You can't have to much power. Horsepower is like cubic inches (and psi of boost  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ): You can never have enough and too many is just right.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><BR><B>12. You can make the Kessel Run in less than 12 parsecs.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"> Whaaaaaaaaaat?....<P><BR>The rest is some funny @#$%||||reg||1
Z||000004||Raydar||01-09-2001||09:54 AM||||The Hot Rodders Rule:<P>If "more" is better, then "too much" is just right.||||reg||12
Z||000005||Shaun41178||01-09-2001||02:40 PM||||an 8.3 C/C is a good ratio for boost and 15 psi isn't that much like Travis said before.  The stock block can handle that much pressure.  but if you are worried about the stock block being the weak point I know where you can get an aluminum racing block  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Not sounding like an @ss but I am going to disagree with Travis with the hyperheutectic pistons and nitrous.  Hyper pistons can handle nitrous just fine in correct air/fuel ratios and of course if you dont' detonate or just use to much nitrous to begin with.  Hyperheutectic pistons are coming stock in almost all cars made today.  The LT1 engines in the 4th gen f-bodies come with hyper pistons from the factory and numerous guys are running nitrous on those cars with no probs.  Some are running 150 hp shots with no probs.<P>What you can do is if you plan to run a turbo you can get hyper pistons and then have them coated on the top to help protect them from the high temps and to keep them from cracking and or melting.  Mike LeCompte(Hyptnotise) on this board can have these done for you.<P>------------------<BR>Shaun 85 GT with nitrous<BR>0-60 in 5.6 seconds<BR><A HREF="http://members.aol.com/Shaun41178" TARGET=_blank>Preferred Performance</A>||||reg||1
Z||000006||DreXteR||01-09-2001||04:26 PM||||1st2m6,  ROLF!  Those jokes are gooooodd!!!  eheheheh  BTW, thnx for da info  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR> <BR>Now I dont have any parts, just making the sketch of what is needed. I dont want to make an error or buy somthing that is not needed.  <P>By now this will the rebuild:<BR>3.2 Flat Pistons, block bored 0.060, 3.1 crank and crank shafts, ported and polish the head cams, SI valves, crane 2030 or similar performance cam, crane valve springs and retainers, ported and polish "the aluminum parts that the injectors connect"(sorry dont know the name of this part)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> , ported manifolds, and maybe aluminum flywheel and kevlar clutch. All dependes in how much will cost.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> The turbine will came later, I just dont want to rebuild it again for the turbo setup.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>If somebody thinks that something is wrong or should change something, please let me know.  I need the advise of the experts.<P>Shaun41178, a aluminum block from a GenIII will work?<P><BR>Thanx  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||10
Z||000007||Will||01-09-2001||05:16 PM||||I read about a Fox mustang with the modern 32V DOHC FoMoCo V8 in it. With a blower and 26 psi of boost it ran 1/4 mi in the 8-9 second range.<P>The interesting thing is that the engine was internally STOCK, hypereutectic pistons and all. When it finally did blow up, they tore it down and found that their 8200 RPM shift points had killed it, not the boost. The piston tops were pristine, but the piston pins had been pulled right out of their bosses! They dropped a new engine in, set the shift points at 7600, dialed in a little more boost and were running the same times as before.<P>The moral of this story: these guys were very careful and conservative with their tuning. They slowly and methodologically approached their tuning. If you do the same, then you can use hypereutectic pistons. If you lack the patience and foresight for this, then get forged pistons, because hyperuetectics won't survive when you put the turbo on.<P>I don't remember where the site is.||||reg||1
Z||000008||mrfixit58||01-09-2001||05:30 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Will:<BR><B>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"> Whaaaaaaaaaat?....<P><BR>The rest is some funny @#$%</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Come on guys!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>The quote: "12. You can make the Kessel Run in less than 12 parsecs." Comes from the original episode of Star Wars.... In the cantina scene Luke and Ben Kanobi have never heard of the Millinium Falcon. Astonished, Han Solo says; "It made the Kessel Run in under 12 parsecs".<P>How young are you guys?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||Will||01-09-2001||05:34 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by mrfixit58:<BR><B> Come on guys!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>The quote: "12. You can make the Kessel Run in less than 12 parsecs." Comes from the original episode of Star Wars.... In the cantina scene Luke and Ben Kanobi have never heard of the Millinium Falcon. Astonished, Han Solo says; "It made the Kessel Run in under 12 parsecs".<P>How young are you guys?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Roy   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I'm 21. Last time I checked a parsec was a unit of distance equal to about 3.26 light years. It's defined as the distance to a star with a paralax of 1 second of arc from one side of the earth's orbit to the other.<P>You can all wake up now.<P>Anyway, I guess I can't expect technical accuracy from a movie...<P>Is that gaff in the books, too?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Pontiaddict||01-09-2001||08:34 PM||||Wasn't there a '71 Corrola in that movie too.<BR>Go George Lucas!||||reg||1
Z||000011||88formula||01-09-2001||10:21 PM||||When you bore your motor over try to bore it as little as possible. The more material you remove from the cylinders the more you weaken the block and the more likely you may have a cooling problem.<P>1FST2M6 id right about the Total Seal Rings. They are a scam. My machinist has an engine dynamometer and he tested them to see if there was an improvement and there was no difference between them and regular molly rings.<P>When the piston is going up and down a bazillion times a second there is no time for a significant amount of gas to escape in my opinion.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000012||88formula||01-09-2001||10:31 PM||||O-yeah I also disagree with Travis about the hypeutectic pistons not being able to withstand nitrous oxide or a turbocharger. My machinist has been building racecar engines for twenty years and he says he uses them all the time in nitrous motors. I also have a Federal Mogul master catalog and it says in the catalog that hyreutectic pistons can be used with a turbocharger or nitrous oxide. If I were going to force 15 lbs. of boost into my motor though I would definitely go with the forged slugs.||||reg||1
Z||000013||88formula||01-09-2001||10:46 PM||||Forgot to say have the engine balanced and the block zero decked and squared. You should also dull any sharp edges in the combustion chambers and piston tops to help prevent pre-ignition.<P>I would also recommend you use the GM Performance 12363220 camshaft. It is the same one used in the GM performance 3.4-liter crate motor and makes more top end power than the Crane 2030. Use the matching springs and retainers too. That is a great camshaft for the 3.2-3.4-liter engines. <P>I have Dyno2000 and Dragstrip2000 so if you want me to test a camshaft for you and tell you were it makes the most power I can do that for you. I can also tell you what to expect for 0-60 and quarter mile times with your setup if I have the right information.<P>E-mail me about the Dyno2000.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000014||DreXteR||01-10-2001||08:41 AM||||88formula, Thanx 4 da info of the GM cam.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>For sure I will email u.<P>I know the factor that more bore less strength.  My concern is if the block will handle the pressure in the cilinders.  The hypernautics will handle 15psi?<BR>BTW, when the turbo setup will came, also I will upgrade the ingectors with GN injectors(or similar), high volume fuel pump, intercooler(i hope).<P>DrexteR<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000015||1FST2M6||01-10-2001||02:00 PM||||Hypereutectic pistons are fine for N/A, Turbo and S/C cars.. they disapate heat GREAT! but they break down with nitrous. I wiped out my 79 vette with Keith Black hypereutectic pistons and all the guys at NOS Inc. said is ".. if you had read your instructions we don't recommend their use, sir..." that was the most expensive phone call i've ever made! they work with nitrous but NOT as well as a "..good forged piston.."  Joe Pettitt, Louis Hammel "Nitrous Oxide Injection Guide: How to make maximum power with nitrous injection" <A HREF="http://www.bn.com" TARGET=_blank>www.bn.com</A>  i purchased that book right AFTER i killed my car. If your spending the $ on pistons get ones you don't have to worry about.  <A HREF="http://www.wiseco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.wiseco.com</A>   not getting mad.. just saying why buy twice... I've already paid for 2 sets of pistons! <P><BR>(for those wondering.. Vermillion on oyster, 402cu.in. fueled by a Holley 900cfm vacuum 3barrel, muncie 4spd(stock) with an NOS plate kit jetted to 100hp(smallest jets in the kit))||||reg||1
Z||000016||DreXteR||01-10-2001||02:42 PM||||Thanx for the advice 1fst2m6.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><BR>DreXteR||||reg||10
Z||000017||Shaun41178||01-10-2001||03:11 PM||||Yes Travis that is kind of the quote I was thinking of.  Hyper pistons can be used with nitrous just not as much nitrous as a forged piston.  Forged will always be stronger then hyper pistons but from an economical standpoint hyper is a good performance piston for a cheap dollar amount.<P>15 lbs of boost is most likely way too much for a hyper piston so if you are 100% for sure that the turbo will go on later then go for the forged.  or get hyper pistons and run around 8-10 pounds of boost.  <P>------------------<BR>Shaun 85 GT with nitrous<BR>0-60 in 5.6 seconds<BR><A HREF="http://members.aol.com/Shaun41178" TARGET=_blank>Preferred Performance</A>||||reg||1
Z||000018||Shaun41178||01-10-2001||03:12 PM||||Oh yea forgot to mention that a Gen 3 block is not made out of aluminum.  A gen 3 block is still cast iron block.  The block I have is a racing style block sold through Gm in the performance parts book.  It can be used in any FWD or RWD application and weighs 50 pounds less then a standard Fiero block.<P>------------------<BR>Shaun 85 GT with nitrous<BR>0-60 in 5.6 seconds<BR><A HREF="http://members.aol.com/Shaun41178" TARGET=_blank>Preferred Performance</A>||||reg||1
Z||000019||1FST2M6||01-10-2001||03:37 PM||||Some one buy Shauns Block! and finish his project!!! SOMEONE here needs an all aluminum motor!! they are VERY rare and special!... you will be way cooler than any V8 here!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 01-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000020||DreXteR||01-10-2001||03:53 PM||||Rolf!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000021||88formula||01-10-2001||04:54 PM||||1FST2M6, what is your opinion on using a 50-75 horsepower shot of nitrous on a 3.4-liter Camaro engine with hyereutectic pistons and a 9.7-1 compression ratio?<P>The difference in power from a .060" bore to a .020" bore is about 1-2 horsepower. If the block flexes too much because there was too much material removed from the cylinders you will lose power because the rings won't seal right. <P><p>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 01-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000022||1FST2M6||01-10-2001||05:06 PM||||you can use nitrous on hyper pistons just not as much as on a forged unit. LS1s run them all day. but with NOS, Nitrous works and the others warning. a stock unit (cast) will with stand a decent shot. I was just unfortunate and had i guess was a bad set of slugs from KB. if your starting from scratch.. get Forged and be done with it.. if you've build the motor or have a stock set up run LOTS of fuel! LOTS!  get the book i mentioned above.. it's $20 and WELL worth it!||||reg||1
Z||000023||Slapnutz2000||01-10-2001||06:21 PM||||Ah man, how can anyone not remember that line from Star Wars?! Now only if the DVD would come out before I turn 60...<P>I know, I know...only a few years...the DVD I mean||||reg||10
Z||000024||Smokin87||01-11-2001||08:55 AM||||There is no such thing as too much power.  the more power you have, the funner the ride!!!||||reg||10
